      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay i get that, but honestly it feels like a lot of those antitrust arguments are just based on outdated theories from decades ago. like, doesn't the fact that everyone uses these services for free or at low cost basically prove they aren't actually hurting consumers? it seems like the whole \"harm to consumer welfare\" thing is kind of a reach in the modern tech era. what do you think, is the antitrust movement actually grounded in reality or is it just political posturing?",
