      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This is a highly debated area, as traditional antitrust frameworks were built around price increases, which isn't always evident in free digital services. A modern counter-argument suggests that \"consumer welfare\" needs to be expanded to include data privacy, algorithmic fairness, and innovation incentives, not just low prices. Therefore, proponents argue that the debate has shifted from simple pricing power to structural market control and influence.",
